    "advancement": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>At 20th level, you can draw strength from the world trees of Azeroth, enlarging your treant shape to equal an ancient as you take on the tranquil shape of a tree of life.</p><p>You can use your action to assume your treant shape and incarnate to a tree of life. For 1 minute, you gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><p>At the start of each of your turns, you gain 10 temporary hit points. When incarnate ends, you lose any remaining temporary hit points.</p></li><li><p>Your size becomes Large, unless you were larger.</p></li><li><p>When you cast a spell that restores hit points to a target, another creature of your choice within 30 feet of it is regains hit points equal to half the amount restored.</p></li></ul><p>The incarnation persists beyond the shapeshift, but has no effect outside of your treant shape. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
